      "id": "api-arda-fardagraphedit-51647141",
      "name": "FArdaGraphEdit",
      "qualifiedName": "arda::FArdaGraphEdit",
      "kind": "class",
      "component": "core",
      "page": "api-reference.html",
      "signature": "class FArdaGraphEdit final",
      "summary": "Begins an exclusive graph edit and records operations in call order. The first authoring failure is retained; later operations do nothing and Commit returns that failure. Cancel and start a new scope to recover. Destruction cancels an uncommitted transaction, preserving the previous executable graph. Never manually end/reopen its transaction while a scope is active. Commit only queues declarations; call Graph.Compile after closing all edits before execution. Graph must outlive this scope. Edits follow the graph's externally synchronized single-owner contract.",
      "details": "Begins an exclusive graph edit and records operations in call order. The first authoring failure is retained; later operations do nothing and Commit returns that failure. Cancel and start a new scope to recover. Destruction cancels an uncommitted transaction, preserving the previous executable graph. Never manually end/reopen its transaction while a scope is active. Commit only queues declarations; call Graph.Compile after closing all edits before execution. Graph must outlive this scope. Edits follow the graph's externally synchronized single-owner contract.",
      "source": "Source/ArdaInfra/ArdaDependencyGraph/Public/Graph/Node/ArdaGraphEdit.h",
      "params": [],
      "returns": "",
      "ownership": "Owning handles retain their object; pointer and reference parameters are borrowed unless stated otherwise.",
      "errors": "Failures and unsupported operations use the declared FArdaRHIStatus or TArdaRHIResult contract.",
      "threading": "Calls follow the synchronization rules of the owning provider device or command list.",
